  "generatedMarkup": "<details class=\"bh-scales\" id=\"bh-scales\" hidden><summary>Real black-hole sizes</summary><ul><li><b>Small stellar · 5 M☉</b><span>Stellar-mass · horizon radius 15 km · shadow radius 38 km</span><small>e.g. <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/universe/nasas-ixpe-reveals-shape-orientation-of-hot-matter-around-black-hole/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Cygnus X-1 source (opens in a new tab)\">Cygnus X-1</a> ≈ 21 M☉<i>Rounded estimate · accreting X-ray binary</i></small></li><li><b>Large stellar · 30 M☉</b><span>Stellar-mass · horizon radius 89 km · shadow radius 230 km</span><small>e.g. <a href=\"https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2024/04/Gaia_black_holes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Gaia BH3 source (opens in a new tab)\">Gaia BH3</a> ≈ 33 M☉<i>Rounded estimate · dormant, no bright disk (unlike the illustrative disk shown here)</i></small></li><li><b>Intermediate · 1,000 M☉</b><span>Intermediate-mass · horizon radius 2,953 km · shadow radius 7,673 km</span><small>e.g. <a href=\"https://dcc.ligo.org/public/0165/P2000021/012/gw190521-implications-main_20200901.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"GW190521 remnant source (opens in a new tab)\">GW190521 remnant</a> ≈ 142 M☉<i>Original 2020 quasi-circular merger model: source-frame median, 90% range +28/−16 M☉</i></small></li><li><b>Galactic core · 1 million M☉</b><span>Supermassive · horizon radius 2,953,250 km · shadow radius 7,672,769 km</span><small>e.g. <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/universe/black-holes/types/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Sagittarius A* source (opens in a new tab)\">Sagittarius A*</a> ≈ 4 million M☉<i>Rounded estimate; precise values differ</i></small></li><li><b>Giant core · 1 billion M☉</b><span>Supermassive · horizon radius 19.7 AU · shadow radius 51.3 AU</span><small>e.g. <a href=\"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/edu/resources/teachable-moment/how-scientists-captured-the-first-image-of-a-black-hole/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"M87* source (opens in a new tab)\">M87*</a> ≈ 6.5 billion M☉<i>Rounded estimate · accretion and jet</i></small></li></ul><p>Radii, not diameters, for a nonspinning black hole of each mass: horizon radius 2GM/c²; apparent shadow radius ≈ 2.6× horizon, as seen from far away. These are not measured image sizes, gas extents or on-screen sizes. Example masses are rounded or model-dependent; follow each link for the source. Disk size is not set by mass. The simulator itself uses model units and softened Newtonian gravity, which is not accurate near a horizon.</p></details>",
